## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Can Find Hub find a phone that is turned off?
A: On supported devices, like the Pixel 8 series, the Find Hub network can still locate the phone for several hours after it's switched off, if offline finding with the network was on. On other phones you see the last known location.

### Q: Can I find my Android phone without an internet connection?
A: Find Hub can show where the phone was when it was last online. If offline finding with the network is on, other Android devices nearby can also report its location over Bluetooth.

### Q: Is Find Hub the same as Find My Device?
A: Yes. Google renamed Find My Device to Find Hub. The website, google.com/android/find, is the same.

### Q: Can I track my stolen phone with the IMEI number?
A: Not yourself. Google describes the IMEI as something your mobile provider can use to disable the phone. Find Hub shows you the IMEI so you can give it to your provider and the police.

### Q: Should I erase my stolen phone?
A: Only when you're sure you won't get it back. Google says a phone that has been factory reset is no longer available in Find Hub, so you can't locate it afterwards. Mark it as lost first.

### Q: Does Find Hub show who has my phone?
A: No. Find Hub shows a location and lets you ring, lock or erase the phone. To get a photo of someone who tries to unlock it, you need an app like CrookCatcher, installed beforehand.

